From 4767842a0f31250b3cd4fc3a99dd869a0c51bac9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt C <latentcollapse@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 05:08:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 29/42] np2: start the NeuraJL kernel with the session, and
 name the call behind elided output

- The kernel starts when the session's tools are built, so its startup
  (about 3s) overlaps the model's first request instead of delaying the
  first call.
- An elision notice says which call's full output Neura.output(n) returns.
- The tool description says workspace packages reload when edited: the
  model's reasonable prior is that a kernel goes stale, which made a julia
  subprocess the rational place to run tests.
- The timeout test asserted the old contract (every timeout stops the
  kernel). Waiting work is now interrupted with the kernel kept; compute
  that never yields still stops it. The test checks both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
